      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3628",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=2\\ln x+x^2-1$, find $f'(x).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\tf'(x) &= \\left(2\\ln x+x^2-1\\right)'\\\n\t\t\t&=2 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}+2x-0\\\n\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{2}{x}+2x.\n\n}\n$$"
    },
