        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1919",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={11}^{x}-5ln⁡x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({11}^{x}-5ln⁡x) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡11-5(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
