        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-11914",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $y=5\\operatorname{ln}x-3{x}^{2}+2x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{ln}x-3{x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{1}{x})-3\\cdot 2x+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x}-6x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
