        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-308854",
        ":question/problem": "Given the function  $y=3{x}^{e}+ln⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{e}+ln⁡x) \\\\  & =3e{x}^{e-1}+\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(3e{x}^{e-1}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =3e\\cdot {1}^{e-1}+\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =3e+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      {
        ":db/id": 17592186314910,
        ":question/answer-fields": [
