        ":question/id": "ff04e1e3-e896-53d9-a3c6-32e3bf7042a0",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-340099",
        ":question/problem": "Given the function  $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2}{x}+{e}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1}+{e}^{1} \\\\  & =2+e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
